# UI design tokens and continuity

## Source rule

Do not use old design docs as authority. The current source of truth is:

- `PRODUCT.md`
- `DESIGN.md` (app-wide visual-language authority)
- `docs/design-system/01-DESIGN-LANGUAGE.md` (DESIGN.md's detailed design companion — gold AI accent, Geist, glass-on-navy)
- `frontend/docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`
- `frontend/src/design-system/`
- `frontend/src/components/ui/`

## Product language

CoachAI is a premium neutral coaching cockpit: evidence-first, operational, compact, accessible, trustworthy, and visually alive through useful hierarchy and module composition.

Role-specific hierarchy is allowed. Role-specific theme drift is not.

## Visual intent target

- 70-80% neutral workspace: platinum canvas, white panels, slate body text.
- 10-15% navy/cobalt: active navigation, selected tabs, primary app actions, key links.
- 5-8% orange: upload/recording intake only.
- 5-8% semantic accents: AI/provenance, progress, risk, approval, evidence confidence.
- 0% random page-local color systems.

Do not overshoot. Avoid all-blue, all-slate, all-white, all-gradient, and private page-theme passes. Inactive nav/tab text should be neutral slate; selected states should be cobalt/navy; upload buttons should use `uploadAction`.

## Reusable UI ownership

Prefer shared primitives for reusable UI:

- `Button`
- `Card` / panel recipe
- `Badge` / status pill / provenance pill
- `SegmentedControl` / tabs
- `EmptyState`
- `PageSkeleton`
- `Toolbar`
- form fields
- dialogs/sheets
- alerts/callouts
- action menus/tooltips

If a page needs a reusable visual pattern, add it to `frontend/src/design-system/recipes.ts` or `frontend/src/components/ui/*` first.

## Banned in new or migrated surfaces

- `.btn-*`
- `.card`
- raw gradient classes
- private arbitrary hex color meanings
- page-local button recipes
- page-local tab recipes
- page-local status badge recipes
- `transition-all`
- spinner-only loading for workspace pages
- raw enum/status labels without human copy
- color-only status meaning
- old bright-blue/navy, purple/indigo, amber CTA, or dark-page theme islands

Dashboard loading and empty states must remain cockpit-shaped with next action, review queue, coaching focus/proof, momentum/risk, and upload intake modules. Blank white panel stacks and spinner-only workspace states are not acceptable.

Legacy classes may remain only as token-backed compatibility wrappers during migration.

## Surface migration mechanism

The UI migrates to the design system one surface at a time. Reusable UI (button/card/**status & provenance pill**/tabs/alert/form/empty-loading) routes to the shared primitives (`Button` / `Panel` / `Badge` / …) backed by semantic roles in `frontend/src/design-system/appDesign.ts` + `foundations.ts` `colorRoles` — never page-local raw status classes. **Migrated files are registered in `scripts/check-ui-guardrails.mjs` `migratedSurfaceFiles`**, which then enforces no raw gradient / `brightBlue` / hex on them. Before restyling or migrating a surface, read `frontend/docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` ("Surface migration") + that script's list. To migrate: route the literals to primitives + roles, delete the raw classes, add the file to `migratedSurfaceFiles`, and re-run `npm run check:ui` + `npm run check:ui-continuity`.

## Route and state continuity

UI work must preserve route state and deep-link context:

- `tab`
- `roleView`
- `repId`
- `userId`
- `sessionId`
- `sandboxId`
- `batchId`
- `candidateId`
- `objection`
- `ts`
- `material`

Dashboard, Team Insights, Call Review, manager approvals, sessions, materials, and improvement plans must not drop context while moving between pages.

## Verification

Run `npm run check:ui-continuity` after UI-system or route work. It should catch stale routes, old visual systems, forbidden shared primitive styles, deep-link param loss, and normal-path use of legacy full-page shells.
